# An Array declared in a nested body has its descriptor in that body's own
# field place. Element stores, element reads and length name it through that
# body; the method's Array of the same name is another place and keeps its
# contents. The root declares one in a nested body too. Entry 7.
fn: check () int
    []: int values 3
    values[0]: 11
    int: seen 0
    if: 1
        []: int values 4
        values[0]: 23
        values[3]: 29
        if: length(values) != 4U || values[0] != 23 || values[3] != 29
            return: 81
        seen: values[3]
    ---
    if: length(values) != 3U || values[0] != 11 || seen != 29
        return: 82
return: 7
int: result check()
if: result = 7
    []: char marks 2
    marks[1]: 'k'
    if: length(marks) != 2U || marks[1] != 'k'
        result: 83
    ---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
